# Experiment Plan

## Research question
How well does a model trained on listings from Global North cities
predict advertised nightly prices in Global South cities?

## City groups
North training cities: New York City, London, Paris
South test cities: São Paulo, Cape Town, Nairobi

## Unit of analysis
One row represents one listing.

## Prediction target
Advertised nightly listing price, converted to USD.
The model will train on log1p of the USD price.

## Primary metric
Mean absolute error in USD.

## Supporting metrics
Median absolute percentage error, RMSE, and R-squared.

## Main experiment
Train and tune using North city listings only.
Test separately on each South city.
Do not use South city prices during training or tuning.

## Planned reference model
Ridge Regression.

## Planned comparisons
Random Forest and Gradient Boosted Trees.

## Planned corrections
1. City relative listing features
2. Importance weighting using target city features only
3. Small labelled target city calibration samples

## Data handling
Raw files remain unchanged in Google Drive.
The GitHub repository contains code, source records, results, and documentation.
